[{"_1":2,"_3":4},"root",{"_5":54},"en/routes/conteudo-do-cubo.tsx",{"_5":6},"data",{"_7":8,"_9":10,"_11":12,"_13":14,"_15":16,"_17":18,"_19":20,"_21":22,"_23":24,"_25":26,"_27":28},"tipo","etapa","cubo",{"_11":52,"_13":52,"_38":53},"id","basico-cruz-amarela","nome","Yellow cross","rascunho",false,"html","<p>The last layer begins. In this step, only the top edges matter: they have to end up with yellow facing up, forming a <a href=\"/en/glossary#cruz\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"The 4 edges of one face (usually white) in place, lined up with the centers. The first step of the beginner method and of CFOP.\">cross</a>. The corners and the side colors are for later.</p>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;3x3&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;R U2 R' U' R U' R'&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;modo&quot;:&quot;eo&quot;}\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/97d3a563b17c0eaa.svg\" alt=\"The goal: the yellow cross (the corners don't matter yet).\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>The goal: the yellow cross (the corners don&#39;t matter yet).</figcaption></figure></div>\n<h2>One algorithm, three shapes</h2>\n<p><code>F R U R&#39; U&#39; F&#39;</code>: the front turns, the <a href=\"/en/glossary#sexy-move\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"The trigger R U R' U', the most common of all.\">sexy move</a> in the middle, and the front comes back.</p>\n<p>Look at the top and see which shape the yellow edges make (the center always counts):</p>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;3x3&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;f U R U' R' f' F U R U' R' F'&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;F R U R' U' F'&quot;,&quot;modo&quot;:&quot;eo&quot;}\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/1ac1f94a3b11a165.svg\" alt=\"**Dot**: no yellow edge. Do the algorithm: it becomes an L.\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption><strong>Dot</strong>: no yellow edge. Do the algorithm: it becomes an L.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"diagrama\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;3x3&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;f U R U' R' f' U2&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;F R U R' U' F'&quot;,&quot;modo&quot;:&quot;eo&quot;}\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/cb92125cab3acc2c.svg\" alt=\"**L**: hold the L at the back left. Do the algorithm: it becomes a line.\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption><strong>L</strong>: hold the L at the back left. Do the algorithm: it becomes a line.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"diagrama\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;3x3&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;F U R U' R' F'&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;F R U R' U' F'&quot;,&quot;modo&quot;:&quot;eo&quot;}\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/f2a951ac5e7c3784.svg\" alt=\"**Line**: hold the line lying down, from left to right. Do the algorithm: it becomes the cross.\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption><strong>Line</strong>: hold the line lying down, from left to right. Do the algorithm: it becomes the cross.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<p>Click a diagram to see the algorithm on the 3D cube. From the dot to the cross, it takes at most 3 times the same algorithm. Before each one, turn the top (<code>U</code>) so the shape is in the right position.</p>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama tira\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;3x3&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;F U R U' R' F'&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;F R U R' U' F'&quot;,&quot;modo&quot;:&quot;eo&quot;}\"><ol aria-label=\"F R U R' U' F'\"><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/0d10a28e0973f63d-0.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>F</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/0d10a28e0973f63d-1.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>R</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/0d10a28e0973f63d-2.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>U</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/0d10a28e0973f63d-3.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>R'</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/0d10a28e0973f63d-4.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>U'</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/0d10a28e0973f63d-5.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>F'</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/0d10a28e0973f63d-6.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"></li></ol><figcaption>From the line to the cross.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Tip:</strong> on a correct cube, there are always 0, 2 or 4 yellow edges facing up. If 1 or 3 show up, an edge is flipped: the cube was taken apart and put back together wrong (or a sticker was swapped), and no algorithm solves it. Take that edge out, flip it and put it back in.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2>Shortcuts</h2>\n<p>The cards of this step show <code>f R U R&#39; U&#39; f&#39;</code> for the L (with <code>f</code>, the two front layers turn together). It takes the L straight to the cross.</p>\n","treino","/3x3/treino?grupo=basico/cruz-amarela/casos","metodos",[47],"anterior",{"_13":45,"_38":46},"proximo",{"_13":43,"_38":44},"grupos",[29],{"_11":30,"_13":14,"_31":32,"_33":34,"_35":16,"_36":37,"_38":39},"Passo 4","nivel","iniciante","casos",3,"conjunto","ids",[40,41,42],"endereco","/3x3/basico/cruz-amarela/casos","B4-Linha","B4-L","B4-Ponto","Yellow face","/3x3/basico/face-amarela","2nd layer","/3x3/basico/segunda-camada",{"_13":48,"_49":50,"_38":51},"Beginner method","numero",6,"/3x3/basico#cruz-amarela","3x3","/3x3/",{"_55":56,"_57":58},"cubos",[61,62,63,64,65,66,67],"idiomas",[59,60],"pt","en",{"_11":52,"_13":52},{"_11":76,"_13":76},{"_11":75,"_13":75},{"_11":74,"_13":74},{"_11":72,"_13":73},{"_11":70,"_13":71},{"_11":68,"_13":69},"skewb","Skewb","pyraminx","Pyraminx","megaminx","Megaminx","5x5","4x4","2x2"]
